+# Hybrid layers: even blocks put ALiBi (Press et al. 2021) on all heads, with the 4-head standard
+# slopes 1/4 .. 1/256 each on two heads; odd blocks get slope 0 on every head, i.e. no positional
+# signal at all (NoPE), so they can look citations up by content at any distance. Same multiset
+# of (head, slope) slots as 115's per-block 4+4 split, arranged by layer instead of by head.
+ALIBI_SLOPES = tuple(2.0 ** (-8.0 * (i // 2 + 1) / 4) for i in range(N_HEAD))
+BLOCK_SLOPES = (ALIBI_SLOPES, (0.0,) * N_HEAD)  # block i uses BLOCK_SLOPES[i % 2]
